ions but  have never appeared in a live-action  film pattinson told collider he's up for  adding robin with conditions yeah but he  has to be 13. that's the only way i'll  accept it no i love death in the family  and stuff but i think it'll be so cool  also people are so scared of it but it's  kind of exciting i think it would be a  really fun addition death in the family  is a 1988 comic story in which the jason  todd version of robin is killed by the  joker todd is an orphan and the second  individual to take up the robin mantle  after dick grayson aged out of it later  todd is resurrected as a vigilante  superhero red hood who unlike batman has  no moral qualms about killing criminals  adjacent todd arc including the  resurrection would seem to fit right in  with the dark tone reeves as  establishing with the batman there's  also the third robin tim drake he's a  third iteration of robin who after  figuring out both batman and robin's  real identities approaches bruce wayne  and asked to become his next sidekick  bruce trains drake into one of the best  martial artists and detectives in the  world drake eventually ages out of the  role too after which she takes on a new  name red robin if reeves really wanted  to throw a curveball he'd go with the  stephanie brown version of robin she's a  street vigilante and the daughter of the  super villain cluemaster who starts her  career as a costumed hero spoiler she  briefly claims a robin mantle but is  fired for disobeying orders she later  becomes bad girl or there's a fifth and  most recent robin damien wayne bruce  wayne's son with talia al gore since  talia appeared in the dark knight rises  and had a brief relationship with bruce  and since the batman is a wholesale  reboot of the franchise this one seems  less likely there's also carrie kelly  from frank miller's the dark knight  returns who spent some time as robin in  a version of batman's very late career  it's also entirely possible that reeves  could follow 